<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Linh Nam chich quai</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">15th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Lĩnh Nam chích quái</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Linh Nam chich quai ('Strange Tales from Linh Nam') is a collection of Vietnamese legends written in classical Chinese, compiled in its surviving form in the 15th century. It tells the origins of the Vietnamese people from Lac Long Quan and Au Co, the Hung kings of Van Lang, and figures such as Thanh Giong and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/an-duong-vuong">An Duong Vuong</a>. It is a main source for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>'s national foundation myths.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/linh-nam-chich-quai.jpg" alt="Linh Nam chich quai" width="320" height="288" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vũ Quỳnh (武瓊), Kiều Phú (喬富) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E5%B6%BA%E5%8D%97%E6%91%AD%E6%80%AA%E5%88%97%E5%82%B3.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
